{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>It was revealed.</b> This thing, and the word 'I' is missing, as in 'YHWH in a vision to him makes Himself known' (Numbers 12:6). And some say that these are the words of the prophet, but the first is correct." "<b>Until you die.</b> By the hand of the enemy besieging you."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {0 "Resolved the omitted subject of 'it was revealed' from context; the comment addresses the impersonal construction."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:54:40.636031830Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}